WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:11.684
TV screens put a store’s live orders, today’s tasks, and who’s on duty on any TV in the shop. In this video, you’ll see what a screen shows, set one up, and connect a TV.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:21.833
Here’s the front counter TV. Open orders sit in columns by stage: new, in progress, and ready for pickup, with the longest wait on top.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:30.288
Anything that’s been waiting too long turns red, so the team can see it from across the room. It updates on its own, every few seconds.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:40.013
In the kitchen, the TV shows today’s tasks and checklists, with a column for each person on duty, each one marked done, now, or overdue.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.123
To set one up, open Order Tracking, or Operations, with a store chosen, and click Show on TV.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:55.609
Name the screen, and tick what it should show: the order board, today’s tasks, who’s on duty. With more than one, the TV takes turns.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:01:07.331
On the TV, open its web browser at your workspace address, followed by slash TV. It shows a short code. Type it here, and the TV switches to your screen in a few seconds.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:14.913
Every screen is listed in Screens and devices, by store. A screen is read-only, and needs no sign-in.

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:21.959
Pick one to see what it’s showing, take a snapshot, set a schedule for when it’s on, or turn it off from here at any time.

